  "worked_solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-5 & =4v+2 \\\\ 9v-5-4v+5 & =4v+2-4v+5 \\\\ 5v & =7 \\\\ v & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $9v-5=4v+2$ has the unique solution $v=\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+3 & =2v+7 \\\\ 2v+3-2v & =2v+7-2v \\\\ 3 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $v.$ Therefore, the equation $2v+3=2v+7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-1 & =5v-1 \\\\ 5v-1-5v & =5v-1-5v \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $v.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
